WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:08.450
Grace Kim: Hi everyone, welcome to the weekly marketing sync. Let's start with the webinar results.

2
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:21.700
Leo Martins: The webinar had six hundred and forty registrations and two hundred and ninety live attendees. That's our best result this year.

3
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:30.950
Grace Kim: Fantastic. How many qualified leads did we get from it?

4
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:44.200
Leo Martins: Eighty two so far. Sales is following up with all of them this week. The replay is getting a lot of views too.

5
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:56.300
Amara Okoye: On the newsletter, open rates went up to forty one percent after we changed the subject line format.

6
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:06.500
Grace Kim: Nice. Amara, can you write a short summary of what we changed so the other teams can reuse it?

7
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.400
Amara Okoye: Sure, I'll post it in the marketing channel tomorrow.

8
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:28.600
Jonas Weber: For SEO, organic traffic is flat this month. Two of our top blog posts dropped in rankings after the search engine update.

9
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:36.800
Grace Kim: What do you need to fix that?

10
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:50.900
Jonas Weber: I'd like to refresh both posts with updated examples and add a comparison table. I'll have the updated drafts ready by next Tuesday.

11
00:01:51.400 --> 00:02:02.700
Leo Martins: I can help with the examples. We have great customer quotes from the webinar that we could use.

12
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:14.000
Grace Kim: Perfect. Leo, please share the webinar quotes with Jonas, and let's review the drafts together on Wednesday.

13
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.200
Grace Kim: Thanks everyone, great week.
